From: Marc Lainez <marc.lainez@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Wake the alert thread every 10 ms instead of 0.5 ms

The alert thread wakes 2000 times a second while any GPIO has edge
detection, about 16% of a CPU on an MSM8974. Edge events still wake it
at once; the timeout only paces the pickup of new alerts and the timing
of debounce and watchdogs, for which 10 ms is enough.

Upstream: not submitted
---
--- a/src/lgPthAlerts.c
+++ b/src/lgPthAlerts.c
@@ -435,7 +435,7 @@
    struct pollfd pfd[64];
    lgAlertRec_p pAlertRec[64];
    struct gpio_v2_line_event eIn[LG_GPIO_MAX_ALERTS_PER_READ];
-   struct timespec tspec = {0, 5e5}; /* 0.5 ms timeout */
+   struct timespec tspec = {0, 1e7}; /* 10 ms timeout */
 
    while (1)
    {
